  "term": "shy–bold continuum",
  "definition": "The shy–bold continuum is a way of describing behavioral types by placing individuals along a range from more shy to more bold. In this source, differences along that range are linked to exploration style and may help explain how individuals differ in their use of space and recurring movements.",
